                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ba710c7a-992c-4e1f-9f4d-33e899eaee09",
                        "source_entry_id": "9cc486f5-479b-3d3f-86a7-ec720b4f2169",
                        "source_sense_id": "3465de1e-f85a-3676-8246-ed52d5c9cdfb",
                        "target_lang_word": "spurge",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "spurge",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "99129bd2-f6fe-3ea0-8b47-9b2c04c81b6d",
                                        "entry_id": "2839cf65-a670-369e-9214-51a7f11f73d5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any plant of the genus Euphorbia, a diverse genus of over 2,000 species."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0e1f2df-9db1-41ca-a20a-7e8c5bc3ef8a",
                                                "sense_id": "99129bd2-f6fe-3ea0-8b47-9b2c04c81b6d",
                                                "text": "But cockle, spurge, according to their law / Might propagate their kind, with none to awe, / You'd think; a burr had been a treasure trove."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6015560e-39f5-4405-af6c-fdf594c673d6",
                                                "sense_id": "99129bd2-f6fe-3ea0-8b47-9b2c04c81b6d",
                                                "text": "A compound of spurge, cardamom, cinnamon of Mecca, pellitory, ginger, nettle seed is an Arab specific for sexual weakness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b8b3bb46-d40b-3815-98b1-ead12b8e08c0",
                                        "entry_id": "2839cf65-a670-369e-9214-51a7f11f73d5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any plant of the spurge family, Euphorbiaceae."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "368feb5c-3983-39de-b7ad-d45015591795",
                                        "entry_id": "2839cf65-a670-369e-9214-51a7f11f73d5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A plant resembling those in genus Euphorbia in some aspect of its appearance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "spurge",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ecf7ebf9-8d99-31ae-9112-f058372dd2d3",
                                        "entry_id": "a7737940-a06f-3ec8-b74b-182cd07a69ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To emit foam; to froth; said of the emission of yeast from beer during fermentation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a52b7a61-6a5f-44af-abad-f4565160896b",
                                                "sense_id": "ecf7ebf9-8d99-31ae-9112-f058372dd2d3",
                                                "text": "The body's somthing noysome: 'tis a stale one; / Good troth it spurgeth very monstrously."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0090edc8-2a9a-4ed3-83a7-3fd30cc17dc1",
                        "source_entry_id": "9cc486f5-479b-3d3f-86a7-ec720b4f2169",
                        "source_sense_id": "3465de1e-f85a-3676-8246-ed52d5c9cdfb",
                        "target_lang_word": "lechetrezna",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lechetrezna",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "961947fd-76fb-352a-8fc8-b4325797506c",
                                        "entry_id": "94ec1b21-40fa-3d9a-9085-bd4bc5795f1b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "(Euphorbia) Planta de la familia de las euforbiáceas, con tallo ramoso de cuatro a cinco cm. de altura, hojas alternas, aovadas, obtusas y serradas por el margen; flores amarillentas en umbelas poco pobladas, fruto capsular con tres divisiones, y semillas menudas y parduscas. Su jugo es lechoso, acre y mordicante y se ha usado en medicina. Hay diversas especies, en general herbáceas."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7dc2134f-9c7f-4fc1-bd6a-18b6d7ad0573",
                                                "sense_id": "961947fd-76fb-352a-8fc8-b4325797506c",
                                                "text": "«Este quejigar, vicariante del gaditano, carece de Ruscus hypophyllus o Clematis cirrhosa, pero, por contra, añade a su inventario una lechetrezna arbustiva endémica (Euphorbia monchiquensis) y la rosa albardera (Paeonia broteri)»."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac0534d5-0321-4eec-8c96-560bc1805311",
                                                "sense_id": "961947fd-76fb-352a-8fc8-b4325797506c",
                                                "text": "«La lenguaza, la romaza;\njugosa, la lechetrezna,\npara pintarse lunares\nla niña que no los tenga»."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
